@startuml
title P1 macOS recording shortcut and menu lifecycle

skinparam shadowing false

actor User
participant "SwiftUI window\nfocused onExitCommand" as Window
participant "Status menu\nvisible while hidden" as Menu
participant "Shell action seam" as Actions
participant "MacRecordingShortcutController\nmain actor + generation" as Controller
participant "Carbon registrar\nRegisterEventHotKey exclusive" as Carbon
participant "Capture controller\n(next integration task)" as Capture

== Configured toggle ==
Controller -> Carbon: register modifier-bearing preset
alt success
  Carbon --> Controller: opaque registration
  Controller --> Window: registered state
else conflict or unsupported
  Carbon --> Controller: typed failure
  Controller --> Window: honest fallback state
  note right of Window
  Window and status-menu buttons
  remain independently available.
  end note
end

User -> Carbon: press configured chord
Carbon -> Controller: hot-key event + generation
Controller -> Actions: toggle recording
Actions -> Capture: start or stop

== Cancel ==
User -> Window: Esc while Pulsar is focused
Window -> Actions: cancel recording
User -> Menu: Cancel recording while window hidden
Menu -> Actions: cancel recording

note over Window,Menu
No global bare-Escape registration.
No NSEvent global key monitor.
No CGEvent tap or Accessibility permission.
end note

== Lifecycle ==
Controller -> Carbon: unregister on reconfigure / sleep / lock / quit
Controller -> Actions: cancel on sleep / lock / quit
Controller -> Carbon: register current preset once on wake / unlock

@enduml
